WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.700
I grew up in this area, in
this very block of flats.

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.200
This is where I spent my school years:

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.200
primary and secondary
school, then high school...

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.800
at Neculce.

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.700
And of course, I went on to sit
the university entrance exam.

6
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.000
And for...

7
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.800
six years, because I did my
degree at evening classes,

8
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.900
I had to make the trip to
the Polytechnic Institute.

9
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.400
Every day I had to cross,

10
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.200
at least twice – once
there, once back –

11
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.500
what we used to call the
Basarab Bridge.

12
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.100
It was actually a
sheet-metal footbridge.

13
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.600
A footbridge with an awful
lot of steps to climb

14
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.600
and an awful lot of steps to go down.

15
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Summer was fairly pleasant – we'd
stop to watch the trains go by.

16
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:03.000
They came through more often then.
Sadly, they don't run as often now.

17
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.000
The problem was winter.

18
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.200
The bridge was made of sheet metal, and
where you walked it was ridged plate.

19
00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:24.000
With so many people going back and
forth, the ridges wore smooth.

20
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:30.200
And in winter, if there was
a frost on top of that,

21
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:37.100
everyone clung to the side of the bridge
and went up and down very carefully.

22
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:42.600
Older people sometimes pulled socks
over their shoes so they wouldn't slip.

23
00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:50.400
For us young ones it was fun –

24
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.400
we'd form a little train to get
up and down the Basarab Bridge.

25
00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.700
Of course, in time it disappeared too,

26
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.500
and this new structure took its place.
